sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2023-glue-19> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "When an ectopic lens is induced in tail tissue by bioelectric modulation, misexpressing the ion channel in only a small subset of the needed cells suffices: these cells recruit unmodified host cells to reach the critical mass for a normal-sized lens, so downstream modules such as size control are activated without micromanagement.";
    dc:type "experimental-result";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "A few bioelectrically induced lens cells recruit host cells to build a normal-sized lens";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Levin M, “Bioelectric networks: the cognitive glue enabling evolutionary scaling from physiology to mind”, Animal cognition (2023), doi:10.1007/s10071-023-01780-3; section “Basal cognition without neurons: what dynamic bodies think about › Navigation: an invariant between morphological, behavioral, and other spaces”. Scope: Xenopus laevis embryos with ion channel misexpression in tail tissue"
}
