sub:quote a prov:Entity;
    prov:hadPrimarySource <https://raw.githubusercontent.com/fractastical/delphisci/2404c437f822e1c98420130cd01e7972acf3ac57/books/levin-papers/inputs/2023-glue.txt#line=67,68>;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/s10071-023-01780-3>;
    <https://schema.org/text> "For example, when an ectopic lens (in tail tissue) is induced by bioelectric modulation, it is sufficient to misexpress the channel only in a small subset of the needed cells: once their organ-level goal is specified, these cells will secondarily recruit other (un-modified) host cells as needed to achieve the critical mass needed to produce a normal-sized lens.".
